103	    <div class="section">
104	      <p>At the core of the gospel is not just forgiveness—it's adoption. God doesn't just save us from sin; He brings us into His family. This means your identity is no longer defined by your past, your performance, or others' opinions, but by the Father who chose you and calls you His own.</p>
105	      <p>Many people live as spiritual orphans—constantly striving for approval, afraid of failure, and unsure of their worth. But in Christ, we are fully known and fully loved. This message invites us to stop performing for identity and start living from it, resting in the truth that we are sons and daughters of God.</p>
